      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue here is that the GPIO is referred to by index, without any reference to the chip.\nIt is possible to create a flat dictionary, I did not think it will make the code much clearer.\nThe best way of course, as you mentioned, is to be able to use the `gpiodetect` `gpiofind` APIs; however, it applies to linux version \u003e 4.8 and the assumption that every gpio is assigned a name, which is a false assumption.",
